            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="0827" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15236.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to Mexico to the Secretary of
                        State ad interim</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-15T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1915—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>642. My 634, June 14, 3 p.m. I have just been assured that 5,000 Villistas under
                    General Medina Veytia are expected in town in two or <pb facs="0828" n="712"
                        xml:id="pg712"/> three days which will increase the possibility of more
                    bloodshed by the conflict between them and Carrancistas. It is the general
                    belief, including the leading diplomatists here who so telegraphed to their
                    Governments, that nothing would contribute more to call the different factions
                    to reason and incline them to settle their differences than an immediate formal
                    and effective prohibition of exportation of arms and ammunition to anybody in
                    Mexico until the end of the trouble.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. M. Cardoso de Oliveira.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
